From: CharlesGool <gzcheng0822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] usb: musb: sprd: release the USB3.1 PLL across system
 suspend

musb_sprd forces the USB3.1 PLL (USB31PLLV) on at probe, because the USB2
PHY takes its 26 MHz reference from it, and never lets go.  Chip-level sleep
(PMU PAD_OUT_CHIP_SLEEP: the 26 MHz crystal off, the rails down) needs every
PLL down, so with the force held the chip never got there: after 136
suspends PAD_OUT_CHIP_SLEEP_EDG_CNT (PMU APB 0xf3c) still read 1, although
the AP, PUB, modem, audio and sensor hub all reached deep sleep, and the
board drew ~19 mA (~73 mW) asleep.  Stock Android, whose musb_sprd.ko turns
the force on and off as needed, counts 1 -> 6 in a single short suspend.

Device-mode system suspend only gets past musb_sprd_pm_suspend() with no
VBUS, so nothing needs the PHY then: drop the force there and put it back
before the PHY is resumed.

Measured on the Rongyue E5 (OpenWrt, 60 s RTC suspends, the force dropped
at syscore suspend): PAD_OUT_CHIP_SLEEP_EDG_CNT 1 -> 5 -> 8; USB enumerates
normally after resume.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_sprd.c	2026-10-17 05:06:45.014393599 +0000
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_sprd.c	2026-10-17 05:06:45.014393599 +0000
@@ -140,6 +140,7 @@
 	struct musb_reg_info		pubsys_bypass;
 	struct musb_reg_info		suspend_clk_src_frc_on;
 	struct musb_reg_info		usb31pllv_frc_on;
+	bool				usb31pllv_released;
 	struct usb_role_switch		*role_sw;
 
 	enum usb_role			role;
@@ -2623,6 +2624,24 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * The USB3.1 PLL is forced on at probe for the USB2 PHY's reference clock,
+ * and a PLL that is forced on keeps the whole chip out of chip-level sleep
+ * (PMU PAD_OUT_CHIP_SLEEP needs every PLL down): with it held, the board
+ * stays at ~19 mA in suspend where it could go far lower.  Device-mode system
+ * suspend only gets this far with no VBUS, so nothing needs the PHY then;
+ * the force goes back on before the PHY is resumed.
+ */
+static void musb_sprd_usb31pllv_frc(struct sprd_glue *glue, bool on)
+{
+	struct musb_reg_info *r = &glue->usb31pllv_frc_on;
+
+	if (!r->regmap_ptr)
+		return;
+	regmap_update_bits(r->regmap_ptr, r->args[0], r->args[1],
+			   on ? r->args[1] : 0);
+}
+
 static int musb_sprd_pm_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct sprd_glue *glue = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -2663,6 +2682,9 @@
 	musb_sprd_suspend(glue);
 	atomic_set(&glue->pm_suspended, 1);
 
+	musb_sprd_usb31pllv_frc(glue, false);
+	glue->usb31pllv_released = true;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -2691,6 +2713,11 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	if (glue->usb31pllv_released) {
+		musb_sprd_usb31pllv_frc(glue, true);
+		glue->usb31pllv_released = false;
+	}
+
 	musb_sprd_resume(glue);
 	atomic_set(&glue->pm_suspended, 0);
 
